# gates_of_heck configuration. All keys optional; delete what you don't use.
GOH_MAX_LINES=500                 # file-length cap; unset disables the check
# GOH_LINE_EXCLUDE='third_party/|\.generated\.'
# GOH_PY_COV_MIN=95
# GOH_SWIFT_MODE=xcode            # or spm
# GOH_SWIFT_SCHEME=MyAppTests
# GOH_SWIFT_COV_MIN=95
# GOH_MAX_SCRATCH_GB=25           # disk-hygiene ceiling (full runs only)

# The skills-corpus gate, run from HERE because nothing else can. The corpus at
# ~/.claude/skills is a global asset with no repo of its own, and this is the
# repo that owns the checker -- so if it is not wired here it is wired nowhere,
# and a gate nobody runs is indistinguishable from a gate that passes. That is
# the exact class check_skills_corpus.py was written to catch, and it was true
# of the checker itself until this line existed.
#
# NOTE the coupling this creates: a commit HERE can now fail because a file
# under ~/.claude/skills is mid-edit. That is deliberate -- the alternative is a
# corpus nothing ever checks -- but it is the reason a commit may go red for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the diff.
GOH_SKILLS_CORPUS=1
GOH_SKILLS_ROOT=$HOME/.claude/skills
